{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098465-newbie-questions","id":1098465,"title":"Newbie Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-30T10:10:12-07:00","id":1098465,"title":"Newbie Questions","content":"Afternoon all,<br /> <br /> I'm relatively new to Mage the Awakening 2e and would be grateful if someone could help me with a few questions (and even more grateful if they can point me to a relevant page). I promise I've googled and searched but no luck.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Potency</b>: If a player increase Scale does the potency apply to each individual or is it divided by them. So suppose a player casts a damaging spell and increases damage to 5 and uses 1 Reach to change Scale to 5 subjects: do they each take 5 damage or 1? I noted under Spell Control (p.118) that it says the spell factors must apply to each equally, which would suggest its the former (5 points). Is that correct?</li> <li><b>Range</b>: Does Mage have to maintain the range for the moment of casting or for the entire duration of the spell? A player in my game cast Animal Minion using 2 reach to cast immediately and at Sensory range. The NPC was however, teleported by another player to an unknown location (out of the sense of the player). Would this have broken the spell or did the Mage only need to sense the subject at the point of casting?</li> <li><b>Spell Control</b>: Does this include attainments such as mage armour?</li> </ol><br /> Thank you for any help in advance<br /> <br /> Akril","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13060-akril","name":"Akril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T10:36:52-07:00","id":1098473,"title":"","content":"1. Potency is applied to all subjects. In your example the entire group of five people would take five damage each.<br /> 2. Only during the casting. Once the spell is cast it mostly lives its own life.<br /> 3. No. Spell control only applies to spells. Neither Arcana Attainments (such as mage armour) nor Legacy Attainments takes up a slot of your spell control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T22:40:54-07:00","id":1098663,"title":"","content":"Your questions were already answered but how did somebody teleport anything to a unknown location, the point of sympathy is that you need to have some form of link to where you teleport something? Was it only unknown to the mage casting Animal Minion?<br /> <br /> Also for 1) remember that if its resisted then the spell might have a different potency vs each person, Ie if a spell potency 5 is withstood by stamina and only 1 person had stamina 5 then 4 people would be effected and 1 person wouldnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T01:40:53-07:00","id":1098693,"title":"","content":"The NPC teleported to a location unknown to the PCs. The NPC probably knew exactly where they teleported.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T08:10:37-07:00","id":1098772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098465-newbie-questions?p=1098693#post1098693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The NPC teleported to a location unknown to the PCs. The NPC probably knew exactly where they teleported.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh just confused me cos he said another player teleported the npc. doesnt matter anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T08:25:06-07:00","id":1098778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098465-newbie-questions?p=1098772#post1098772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh just confused me cos he said another player teleported the npc. doesnt matter anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. It was I who misread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T08:35:47-07:00","id":1098781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098465-newbie-questions?p=1098778#post1098778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. It was I who misread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disentangling the paragraph, it seems to be that PC 1 cast Animal Minion on an NPC, then PC 2 teleported that same NPC somewhere unknown to PC 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:41:57-07:00","id":1098872,"title":"","content":"Whoops. Sorry for causing the confusion (although it seems to have provided some Sherlock amusement). PC1 cast animal dominion on NPC. PC2 (who is acting against PC1) then teleported the NPC away in order to break PC1's spell by moving them out of sensory range.<br /> <br /> Thank you Tessie for your help. In relation to question 2, I note the rules on concentration appear to have been changed. So for example for Telekinisis, if a Mage is no longer able to concentrate on the subject the spell continues but the object becomes suspended. Would this not be the same for any spell requiring concentration (including Animal Minion) and would it therefore imply that you would need to retain a sensory connection (how can you control something you cannot see). The spell would still be in effect but unless and until you can see them again you cannot utilise the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13060-akril","name":"Akril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:52:48-07:00","id":1098879,"title":"","content":"You could still force the minion to take bodily actions, but that's going to be of limited use if you can't see the results, or if it was even able to successfully accomplish the action. I don't need to see my minion John Smith to make him pick his nose. But I'll have no idea if he was actually able to - he could be physically restrained for all I know.<br /> <br /> Navigation would be similarly hampered. 'Walk forward' is easy. &quot;Walk to this place&quot; is harder if not impossible without access to sensory input.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (how can you control something you cannot see). </div> </div> </div>Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T23:07:51-07:00","id":1099033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098465-newbie-questions?p=1098879#post1098879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could still force the minion to take bodily actions, but that's going to be of limited use if you can't see the results, or if it was even able to successfully accomplish the action. I don't need to see my minion John Smith to make him pick his nose. But I'll have no idea if he was actually able to - he could be physically restrained for all I know.<br /> <br /> Navigation would be similarly hampered. 'Walk forward' is easy. &amp;quot;Walk to this place&amp;quot; is harder if not impossible without access to sensory input.<br /> <br /> <br /> Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animal Minion puts you in the driver seat of another's body and renders your own body inert. I assume you can use their eyes. Heck, this scenario would effectively teleport the consciousness of the Mage who cast Animal Minion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T05:16:42-07:00","id":1099120,"title":"","content":"Your operating the person like a puppet, you can force them to move their eyes but your not using their eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T05:52:09-07:00","id":1099127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098465-newbie-questions?p=1099120#post1099120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your operating the person like a puppet, you can force them to move their eyes but your not using their eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd disagree with that considering the state it puts your own body in while the spell is active rendering you inert and only semi-aware of your own surroundings. This is a spell you go to when you want a puppet that you can walk into a situation where you wouldn't want your own body meaning distance traversed shouldn't matter, and you must be able to maintain sensory information from the body you're jacking. Heck, you could argue that since your level of control is so complete you'd have to be receiving that information anyway or you wouldn't have any way of knowing if you've remembered to keep them breathing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}